    "intro_html":  "Caldereta is the Filipino special occasion stew, the one that shows up at birthdays and fiestas. Beef braises with potatoes, carrots, and peppers in a tomato base, and then two things go in that surprise everyone the first time: peanut butter and cheese. They are not a gimmick. They thicken the sauce and give it a savory richness that tomato alone cannot reach. Each bowl lands at 855 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e61 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$7.61 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
